{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Resource Allocation — PF Regeneration and Softmax Dynamics\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo examines the resource allocation phase under four parameter scenarios. Each scenario runs 30 daily iterations and observes resource regeneration, softmax allocation weights, and PF (protective factor) efficacy trajectories.\n",
        "\n",
        "The theory predicts: regeneration is inversely proportional to current resources (`R' = base_regeneration × (1 − R) × affect_mult × resilience_mult`); high softmax temperature produces near-uniform allocation, low temperature produces winner-take-most; PF efficacy gains follow diminishing returns as efficacy approaches 1.0.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "8c3f278a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from numpy.random import Generator, PCG64\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.phases.resource_allocation import run_phase\n",
        "\n",
        "_FACTORS = [\"social_support\", \"family_support\", \"formal_intervention\", \"psychological_capital\"]"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Four Scenarios\n",
        "\n",
        "Each scenario tests a different regime of resource level and softmax temperature."
      ],
      "id": "60f18a00"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: scenarios\n",
        "N_DAYS = 30\n",
        "BASE_REGENERATION = 0.1\n",
        "IMPROVEMENT_RATE = 0.1\n",
        "\n",
        "scenarios = {\n",
        "    \"High R + default T\": {\"resources\": 0.8, \"temperature\": 1.0, \"efficacies\": {f: 0.5 for f in _FACTORS}},\n",
        "    \"Low R + default T\":  {\"resources\": 0.2, \"temperature\": 1.0, \"efficacies\": {f: 0.5 for f in _FACTORS}},\n",
        "    \"High R + high T\":    {\"resources\": 0.8, \"temperature\": 5.0, \"efficacies\": {f: 0.5 for f in _FACTORS}},\n",
        "    \"Varied starting PF\": {\"resources\": 0.5, \"temperature\": 1.0, \"efficacies\": {\"social_support\": 0.9,\n",
        "                           \"family_support\": 0.3, \"formal_intervention\": 0.5, \"psychological_capital\": 0.2}},\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "all_records = []\n",
        "trajectories = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for scenario_name, params in scenarios.items():\n",
        "    state = {\n",
        "        \"resources\": params[\"resources\"], \"affect\": 0.0, \"resilience\": 0.5,\n",
        "        \"protective_factors\": dict(params[\"efficacies\"]),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    config = {\"base_regeneration\": BASE_REGENERATION,\n",
        "              \"softmax_temperature\": params[\"temperature\"],\n",
        "              \"protective_improvement_rate\": IMPROVEMENT_RATE}\n",
        "    efficacies_traj = {f: [] for f in _FACTORS}\n",
        "    rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
        "\n",
        "    for day in range(N_DAYS):\n",
        "        out = run_phase(state, config, rng)\n",
        "        obs = out[\"observation\"]\n",
        "        for f in _FACTORS:\n",
        "            state[\"protective_factors\"][f] = obs[\"efficacies_after\"][f]\n",
        "        state[\"resources\"] = out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"resources\", state[\"resources\"])\n",
        "        state[\"affect\"] *= 0.95\n",
        "        all_records.append({\n",
        "            \"scenario\": scenario_name, \"day\": day,\n",
        "            \"regeneration_amount\": obs[\"regeneration_amount\"],\n",
        "            \"allocation_weights\": obs[\"allocation_weights\"],\n",
        "            \"resources_after\": state[\"resources\"],\n",
        "            **{f\"pf_{f}\": obs[\"efficacies_after\"][f] for f in _FACTORS},\n",
        "            **{f\"weight_{f}\": obs[\"allocation_weights\"].get(f, 0) for f in _FACTORS},\n",
        "        })\n",
        "        for f in _FACTORS:\n",
        "            efficacies_traj[f].append(obs[\"efficacies_after\"][f])\n",
        "    trajectories[scenario_name] = efficacies_traj\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(all_records)\n",
        "print(f\"Generated {len(df)} records across {len(scenarios)} scenarios\")"
      ],
      "id": "scenarios",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Per-Scenario Correlogram"
      ],
      "id": "711f2417"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-correlogram\n",
        "corr_vars = [\"regeneration_amount\", \"resources_after\", \"pf_social_support\",\n",
        "             \"pf_family_support\", \"pf_formal_intervention\", \"pf_psychological_capital\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "for scenario_name in scenarios:\n",
        "    sub = df[df[\"scenario\"] == scenario_name][corr_vars]\n",
        "    g = sns.PairGrid(sub, diag_sharey=False)\n",
        "    g.map_upper(sns.scatterplot, s=10, alpha=0.5)\n",
        "    g.map_lower(sns.scatterplot, s=10, alpha=0.5)\n",
        "    g.map_diag(sns.kdeplot, fill=True)\n",
        "    g.fig.suptitle(f\"Scenario: {scenario_name}\", y=1.02, fontsize=12)\n",
        "    plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-correlogram",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 3: PF Efficacy Trajectories"
      ],
      "id": "c5486a00"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-timeseries\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(10, 8))\n",
        "colors = [\"#3498db\", \"#e74c3c\", \"#2ecc71\", \"#f39c12\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "for idx, (scenario_name, traj) in enumerate(trajectories.items()):\n",
        "    ax = axes[idx // 2, idx % 2]\n",
        "    days = np.arange(N_DAYS)\n",
        "    for fi, f in enumerate(_FACTORS):\n",
        "        ax.plot(days, traj[f], label=f, color=colors[fi], linewidth=1.5)\n",
        "    ax.set_title(scenario_name, fontsize=10)\n",
        "    ax.set_xlabel(\"Day\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"PF Efficacy\")\n",
        "    ax.legend(fontsize=7); ax.set_ylim(0, 1.05)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.suptitle(\"PF Efficacy Trajectories Across Scenarios\", fontsize=13)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-timeseries",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What We See\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Regeneration** is higher when resources are low (diminishing returns). Low-R scenarios show larger regeneration spikes.\n",
        "- **Softmax temperature**: T=5 produces near-uniform allocation; T=1 concentrates resources on high-efficacy factors (rich-get-richer).\n",
        "- **Varied starting PF**: the social_support factor (initially 0.9) receives the largest allocation share, reinforcing its lead.\n",
        "- **Diminishing returns**: PF efficacy growth slows as each factor approaches 1.0, consistent with `Δe_f ∝ (1 − e_f)`.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Resource allocation determines how agents invest their protective factors over time. The softmax temperature parameter directly controls the trade-off between exploration (uniform allocation) and exploitation (focus on strengths). The regeneration dynamics ensure that depleted resources recover, preventing agents from getting permanently stuck in low-resource states. This phase is critical for long-run simulation stability."
      ],
      "id": "33c513c1"
    }
  ],
